# Statistical & ML Analysis Toolkit

A Streamlit-based GUI for end-to-end statistical and machine learning analysis. Designed for researchers working with tabular CSV data, the toolkit chains data ingestion, cleaning, analysis, and visualization into a single point-and-click interface — no scripting required at runtime.

Developed by Liam Sweeney.

---

## Features

### Statistical Analyses
- **Uni/Multivariate Exploration** — descriptive statistics and distributional summaries across one or more variables, exported to CSV
- **Repeated Measures ANOVA & ICC** — within-subjects ANOVA via `pingouin`, with intraclass correlation and six post-hoc correction methods (Bonferroni, Šidák, Holm, FDR-BH, FDR-BY, uncorrected)
- **Chi-Square Test** — association testing between categorical dependent and independent variables

### ML Analyses
- **Gaussian Mixture Model (GMM)** — unsupervised clustering with automated model selection; fits all four covariance types (`full`, `tied`, `diag`, `spherical`) across K = 1–10 and selects the best configuration via BIC (1-SD rule); outputs NMI, ARI, cluster proportions, and LDA cross-validated accuracy
- **Ordinary Least Squares Regression (OLSR)** — linear regression with residual diagnostics
- **OLS Moderated Regression Analysis (MRA) + Simple Slopes** — mean-centered interaction modeling with Breusch-Pagan heteroscedasticity check and simple slope probing at ±1 SD
- **Binary Logistic Regression (BLR)** — logistic regression with auto-dichotomization, odds ratios with 95% CIs, McFadden pseudo-R², and assumption warnings (class imbalance, events-per-predictor)
- **BLR Moderated Regression Analysis (MRA) + Simple Slopes** — interaction modeling on a binary outcome with the same simple slopes framework as OLS MRA
- **Ordinal Logistic Regression (OLR)** — for ordered categorical outcomes
- **Negative Binomial Regression (NBR)** — for overdispersed count outcomes

### Data Visualizations
- **Descriptive** — distribution plots per selected variable
- **Heatmap** — correlation heatmap across selected variables
- **PairGrid** — pairwise relationship grid with KDE overlays
- **PairPlot** — seaborn pairplot with KDE on diagonals

### Full-Data Generators
- **Master Descriptive CSV Generator** — one summary CSV covering all variables in the dataset
- **All Variable Descriptives Generator** — per-variable descriptive CSVs for the full dataset

### Data Utilities
- **File Type Converter** — converts non-CSV files (e.g., SPSS `.sav`) to CSV
- **CSV Merger** — merges all CSVs placed in `files/unmerged_csvs/` into a single master CSV

---

