---

## Notes

- The GMM pipeline applies PCA before clustering, retaining components that explain ≥ 95% of variance. Model selection uses the BIC 1-SD rule across all covariance structures and K values.
- MRA pipelines mean-center predictors and moderators before computing the interaction term to reduce multicollinearity.
- BLR auto-dichotomizes count DVs (any occurrence vs. none) and emits warnings for class imbalance and insufficient events-per-predictor.
- Missing value codes defined in `config.py` are recoded to `NaN` at load time. Variables listed in `IMPOSSIBLE_ZERO_VARS` have zero values treated as missing prior to analysis.
